T.append(L(P+"t03","Spring Boot AOP","medium",
"Aspect-Oriented Programming (AOP) in Spring Boot separates cross-cutting concerns such as logging, security and transactions into aspects applied to methods through pointcuts.",
"AOP me logging, security jaisi common cheezein alag 'aspect' me likhte hain aur pointcut se batate hain kis methods par lagani hain. spring-boot-starter-aop add karo, @Aspect class likho.",
"A security guard at the gate who checks everyone entering any room, instead of each room doing its own checks.",
"@Aspect @Component class LogAspect { @Before(\"execution(* com.demo.service.*.*(..))\") void log(JoinPoint jp){ System.out.println(\"Calling \" + jp.getSignature()); } }",
["Concepts: aspect, advice, join point, pointcut, weaving.","Advice types: @Before, @After, @AfterReturning, @AfterThrowing, @Around.","Pointcut expression: execution(modifiers return pkg.Class.method(args)).","Implemented via runtime proxies (JDK dynamic/CGLIB).","Starter: spring-boot-starter-aop.","Use for logging, timing, security, transactions."],
["AOP terms.","Five advice types.","Pointcut example."],
["Define AOP terms.","Write a logging aspect.","Pick advice type."],
["Calling an advised method from inside the same class (proxy bypassed).","Forgetting @Component on the aspect."],
[E("conceptual","Explain AOP with terms and example.","Aspect, advice, pointcut, join point, weaving; logging aspect."),
 E("difference","@Before vs @Around.","@Before runs before the method; @Around wraps the call and can control it.")],
[Q("MCQ","Advice that wraps the method:","@Around","",["@Before","@After","@Around","@AfterThrowing"]),
 Q("true/false","Spring AOP uses proxies.","True",""),
 Q("short answer","What is a pointcut?","An expression selecting join points where advice applies.",""),
 Q("scenario","Log execution time of all service methods. Use?","@Around aspect",""),
 Q("comparison","Aspect vs advice.","Aspect is the module; advice is the action inside it.","")],
"AOP: aspect/advice/pointcut/join point; @Before/@After/@AfterReturning/@AfterThrowing/@Around; proxy-based; starter-aop.",
syntax="@Aspect @Component class X { @Before(\"execution(* com.demo.service.*.*(..))\") void log(){…} }",
code="@Aspect\n@Component\npublic class LogAspect {\n  @Around(\"execution(* com.demo.service.*.*(..))\")\n  public Object time(ProceedingJoinPoint pjp) throws Throwable {\n    long t = System.currentTimeMillis();\n    Object r = pjp.proceed();\n    System.out.println(pjp.getSignature() + \" took \" + (System.currentTimeMillis()-t) + \" ms\");\n    return r;\n  }\n}",
expectedOutput="OrderService.place(..) took 12 ms",
codeExplanation="The around advice measures time around proceed(), applying to all service methods without changing them.",
apis=["@Aspect","@Before","@After","@Around","JoinPoint","ProceedingJoinPoint"],
commonErrors=["Aspect not applied: missing @Component or starter-aop.","Self-invocation not intercepted."]))
