"Spring REST builds RESTful web services with @RestController and HTTP-method annotations, exchanging JSON and mapping GET, POST, PUT and DELETE to read, create, update and delete operations.",
"Spring REST me controller JSON return karta hai (@RestController). HTTP methods ke hisaab se CRUD: GET=read, POST=create, PUT=update, DELETE=delete. Postman ya curl se test karte hain.",
"A vending machine with fixed buttons: each button (HTTP verb + URL) triggers one standard action and returns a standard response (JSON).",
"GET /students → list; GET /students/1 → one; POST /students (JSON body) → create; PUT /students/1 → update; DELETE /students/1 → remove, returning proper status codes.",
["@RestController = @Controller + @ResponseBody.","@GetMapping, @PostMapping, @PutMapping, @DeleteMapping, @RequestMapping.","@PathVariable reads URL parts; @RequestBody reads JSON; @RequestParam reads query.","ResponseEntity sets status and headers (200, 201, 404, 204).","JSON conversion via Jackson automatically.","REST principles: stateless, resource URLs, uniform interface."],
